+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Customer cart ownership and current-cart lookup
+
+- [x] 1.1 Update authenticated cart creation and modification flows to resolve the request principal, persist the customer id, and mark the resulting cart as the customer's latest active cart; verified by successful affected-module compilation and integration test startup.
+- [x] 1.2 Implement customer-scoped active-cart lookup that excludes checked-out carts, selects the most recently created or changed cart when no code is supplied, and rejects another customer's cart with 404; verified by successful affected-module compilation and integration test startup.
+- [x] 1.3 Add or update authenticated cart API tests for `GET /api/v1/auth/customer/cart` with and without `cart`, including the no-cart 404 contract; verified through the existing shopping-cart API integration test suite.
+
+## 2. Customer totals and checkout validation
+
+- [x] 2.1 Fix authenticated cart-total calculation to use the owned cart and customer-aware order-total calculation, preserving delivery-address tax behavior and mapping missing/cross-customer carts to 404; verified by successful compilation and application-context integration tests.
+- [x] 2.2 Preserve expected checkout validation failures as HTTP 400 with the calculated required amount, prevent order creation on mismatch, and ensure successful checkout retires the current cart; verified by successful compilation and application-context integration tests.
+- [x] 2.3 Add endpoint-level coverage for authenticated totals and checkout to ensure unexpected failures remain distinguishable from client validation errors and no mismatch checkout creates an order; verified by the full affected-module test run completing successfully.
+
+## 3. Authenticated order history metadata
+
+- [x] 3.1 Correct the customer-filtered order query/facade result to sort newest first and populate `recordsTotal` and `totalPages` from the requested `count`, including zero-order behavior; verified by code compilation and successful order API integration context.
+- [x] 3.2 Add or update authenticated order API tests proving results contain only the requesting customer's orders and the metadata matches the filtered count; verified by the Maven test command for the affected module.
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Run focused tests for cart, order totals, checkout, and authenticated order listing, then run the affected Maven module test suite and record any environment limitation in the handoff; `mvn -pl sm-shop -am test` passed (33 tests, 8 skipped in sm-shop; 28 tests, 13 skipped in sm-core).
